**Lemma 3.2 (actual four-history average).** For every $0<x<c$ put

$$
\bar\rho_x=\tfrac14\sum_{\beta\in\{0,\pi\},\ m\in\{0,1\}}
\rho_{x,\beta,m}.
\qquad
\bar\rho_x=2xP_++2(c-x)P_-+ZP_2.
\tag{AC.7}
$$

In particular $x\mapsto\bar\rho_x$ is affine.

Proof. The two values of $e^{-i\beta}$ cancel every middle-to-bottom
matrix entry. The two parities cancel the plus-to-minus entry. The three
diagonal entries are the displayed squared amplitudes. Every summand has
the common-preparation realization of Proposition 3.1. Averaging is a
mathematical source witness; it gives the processor neither four specimens,
the nuisance labels nor a measured probability law. $\square$

